{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102981-favorite-nwod-cofd-books-and-why","id":1102981,"title":"Favorite nWod/CofD books, and why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-12T18:58:40-07:00","id":1102981,"title":"Favorite nWod/CofD books, and why?","content":"I've got a good bit of core nWod books (about ten or so) but I'm looking to expand my collection. Instead of just asking &quot;so, what book should I get next?&quot; I figured I would ask what your favorite 3-5 books of the core line are and why.<br /> <br /> My favorite supplements are biased on the type of game I like to run. My game world is more or less &quot;normal&quot; and so are the characters. While they might be really good investigators, fighters, or con men, they fall within the realistic spectrum of &quot;normal humans.&quot; That might change, though, as I'm considering expanding into some more &quot;superhuman&quot; ideas (through the use of supernatural merits and such). This circles back to my intent of this thread - to see what supplements others lIke and why.<br /> <br /> For me:<br /> <br /> 1) Hurt Locker - really expands normal humans with updated merits. I also like the new conditions.<br /> <br /> 2) Tales of the 13th Precent - as my games are centered around normal people, law enforcement plays a major role. This book fleshes out LE pretty good.<br /> <br /> 3) Slasher - awesome book for serial killing, deranged &quot;normal&quot; foes. <br /> <br /> 4) Second Sight - I haven't used this one a lot, yet, but as my games might begin to push into the &quot;extraordinary&quot; realm, this book is nice. I really like the low level psychics and mages that this supplement introduces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T19:26:37-07:00","id":1102992,"title":"","content":"Core. Lets see. I generally like people to have options that can supplement their player abilities. I don't force them to pick it but if someone is the descendant of a family of hyena cultists, it's nice to have something mechanical I can give them to represent it. These things tend to work on the other side of things, as well, where the players might look at ravaged corpses and expect to deal with a werewolf only to find silver doesn't affect the hyena-woman. An incredibly unsubtle example, my players are in the Neolithic right now and there's a 'tribe' of people called the Blood Drinkers who are eschewing the whole agricultural fad in favor of something much darker. Between the name and the rumors that they only hunt at night, they're thinking vampires, but they just stumbled upon some of their traps and are finding them to be something else.<br /> <br /> Inferno, because it has a nice mix of storyteller and player options, as well as assorted bad guys and regular NPCs to throw into things.<br /> <br /> The Book of Spirits, which is incredibly useful as a werewolf fan and someone generally interested in the spirit side of things. It has some info not available across the werewolf books and shows the Hisil from the perspective of the mortals that occasionally stumble into it and are all-too-often victims of its inhabitants.<br /> <br /> Asylum. I'd probably throw in 13th Precinct if you hadn't already. There's a few of these books that show the Chronicles of Darkness from the perspective of some of its major inhabitants. Precinct gives you law enforcement, Dogs of War the military, and Asylum the medical health field. In addition to helping players and Storytellers both flesh out their characters, they often show how to put these characters into scary situations. Asylum and Precinct also offer a specific setting, with the 13th Precinct and Asylum's Bishopsgate Hospice and Asylum, complete with inmates. I was hoping there would be more in this vein. One perhaps for politics and business, another for organized and disorganized criminals.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers, I think, really helps when it comes to throwing the weird into games. It seems like a simple concept, people who change into animals, but it offers a lot to go beyond that. A man who can turn into a swarm of ants, a lab rat with malign human intelligence, evil birds that watch over a wealthy and decadent family. Any game would easily be able to take one creature from it, but even if they didn't want to there's a system and advice inside for designing new monsters. In the same vein I like Immortals but I think it doesn't offer as many player-friendly options as Skinchangers does.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it counts for core, but Dark Eras, too. Great settings for a variety of games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T01:13:35-07:00","id":1103038,"title":"","content":"Danse Macabre is an absolute triumph of evocative writing and I'm devastated that Atrocity Dice didn't make it into core. Book of the Deceived is also just an absolute treat to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:06:54-07:00","id":1103183,"title":"","content":"I started collecting NWoD/CofD books a few months ago, and read a handful and would have to say my two favorites are the Blue Book/World of Darkness 1st ed and Changeling the Lost (which I am only 45 pages in but friggin love it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:13:28-07:00","id":1103215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102981-favorite-nwod-cofd-books-and-why?p=1102992#post1102992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asylum. I'd probably throw in 13th Precinct if you hadn't already. There's a few of these books that show the Chronicles of Darkness from the perspective of some of its major inhabitants. Precinct gives you law enforcement, Dogs of War the military, and Asylum the medical health field. In addition to helping players and Storytellers both flesh out their characters, they often show how to put these characters into scary situations. Asylum and Precinct also offer a specific setting, with the 13th Precinct and Asylum's Bishopsgate Hospice and Asylum, complete with inmates. I was hoping there would be more in this vein. One perhaps for politics and business, another for organized and disorganized criminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have and like all three of these. I think they're good at fleshing out the darker aspects of their respective specialties and, with my games being less extraordinary, also at adding in some modern &quot;realistic&quot; antagonists/snags into chronicles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inferno, because it has a nice mix of storyteller and player options, as well as assorted bad guys and regular NPCs to throw into things.<br /> <br /> The Book of Spirits, which is incredibly useful as a werewolf fan and someone generally interested in the spirit side of things. It has some info not available across the werewolf books and shows the Hisil from the perspective of the mortals that occasionally stumble into it and are all-too-often victims of its inhabitants.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers, I think, really helps when it comes to throwing the weird into games. It seems like a simple concept, people who change into animals, but it offers a lot to go beyond that. A man who can turn into a swarm of ants, a lab rat with malign human intelligence, evil birds that watch over a wealthy and decadent family. Any game would easily be able to take one creature from it, but even if they didn't want to there's a system and advice inside for designing new monsters. In the same vein I like Immortals but I think it doesn't offer as many player-friendly options as Skinchangers does. </div> </div> </div>As my games progress down more extraordinary avenues, I've been contemplating picking up these three books as well, and also Immortals and Changing Breeds. I am also considering Reliquary, too, because I think items as a source of extraordinary power fits well into the game I'm trying run (and I've been heavily inspired by Stan Lee's <i>Lucky Man</i>, a British television series, where the protagonist has a bracelet that grants him luck).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:22:44-07:00","id":1103219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChristopherZacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102981-favorite-nwod-cofd-books-and-why?p=1103183#post1103183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started collecting NWoD/CofD books a few months ago, and read a handful and would have to say my two favorites are the Blue Book/World of Darkness 1st ed and Changeling the Lost (which I am only 45 pages in but friggin love it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a dyed in the wool fantasy gamer, but my second favorite genre is modern. I like modern crime, horror, supers, espionage, and action, and I've done a pretty good job (I think) putting those together into a modern campaign. Well, the &quot;supers&quot; and &quot;horror&quot; hasn't shown up yet, but it's beginning to. And I really like nWoD for this game. I've tried/considered other systems, but nWoD/CoD just does a really good job, I haven't gotten into the specific core books (Vampire, Mage, Changeling, etc.) and I don't think I will (because primarily supernatural/horror isn't my game) but I'm sure they're well written as well. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:40:48-07:00","id":1103225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Dynel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102981-favorite-nwod-cofd-books-and-why?p=1103219#post1103219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a dyed in the wool fantasy gamer, but my second favorite genre is modern. I like modern crime, horror, supers, espionage, and action, and I've done a pretty good job (I think) putting those together into a modern campaign. Well, the &quot;supers&quot; and &quot;horror&quot; hasn't shown up yet, but it's beginning to. And I really like nWoD for this game. I've tried/considered other systems, but nWoD/CoD just does a really good job, I haven't gotten into the specific core books (Vampire, Mage, Changeling, etc.) and I don't think I will (because primarily supernatural/horror isn't my game) but I'm sure they're well written as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm huge fan or roleplaying because of horror based systems. I don't have a huge history of roleplaying but the history I do have is will White Wolf games. Vampire: The Masquerade was the only game I had ran, and I always ran it in the personal/eerie horror type, rather than the big metaplot type. When I started talking about wanting to run a mortal game, someone from my group recommended NWoD - World of Darkness 1st ed and I feel in love with it. Now I run a horror game called the Ultimate Evil on my channel that takes place in 1986, Bismarck North Dakota and deals somewhat with the Satanic Panic of the 80s.<br /> <br /> I can attest though, as a horror fan, that Changeling the Lost is the most horrific game core book I have read. The whole concept is eerie, scary, and just mentally fucked up, and I love every bit of it. Someone from our group will be running a Changeling game soon and I am super excited for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T05:18:52-07:00","id":1103774,"title":"","content":"Anyone else feel like contributing? I'm interested in hearing others' opinions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T05:52:23-07:00","id":1103778,"title":"","content":"I like having the most content under one book, so Second Sight (3 systems for supernatural powers), Immortals (a bunch of immortal types and their subsystems), Inferno (Possessed and Indebted, plus supporting systems), and even Antagonists to some degree, are some favorites.<br /> <br /> Edit: and Mirrors, hands down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T07:09:18-07:00","id":1103795,"title":"","content":"I haven't read much, but maybe Astral Realms? I <i>really</i> like &quot;journey into the mind&quot; type stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T12:17:57-07:00","id":1103876,"title":"","content":"I have a soft spot for Innocents. I don't have many basic &quot;blue book&quot; supplements, but Asylum is a pretty good and creepy read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:41:35-07:00","id":1104088,"title":"","content":"<b>Mirrors </b>is top notch, and it would take me years to mine even a fraction of all the cool stuff in <b>Book of the Dead</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T19:13:43-07:00","id":1104107,"title":"","content":"I'm seconding <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, Mummy is my favourite game line in general and the revelations about the Sixth Guild were pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Midnight Roads is right up there too, though my current Promethean game is my first time trying out a &quot;travel&quot; based Chronicle. I'd absolutely love to see an equivalent looking at the many different ways people travel by sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T20:00:53-07:00","id":1104123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102981-favorite-nwod-cofd-books-and-why?p=1104107#post1104107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm seconding <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, Mummy is my favourite game line in general and the revelations about the Sixth Guild were pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Midnight Roads is right up there too, though my current Promethean game is my first time trying out a &amp;quot;travel&amp;quot; based Chronicle. I'd absolutely love to see an equivalent looking at the many different ways people travel by sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely forgot how good Midnight Roads is. Absolutely my favorite blue book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T10:51:17-07:00","id":1104365,"title":"","content":"Slashers. The inclusion of themed serial killers has become standard in games I run. I got inspired to do that watching American Horror Story, which, no matter what the story is that season, always has one or more slashers, who are sometimes also the protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:25:22-07:00","id":1104386,"title":"","content":"Ammm.. that's an hard choice. Ancient Bloodlines is beautiful, full of awesome setting material and player options. Immortals has a great concept and it explores it through some fascinating channels. Inferno is simply awesome, from the way it presents Hell and demons and up to the Possessed template and the Lucifuge's evil counterparts. Talking about the Lucifuge, Hunter deserves more than a mention, as it is my favorite gameline- and my favorite book in the line is Witch Finders. The Gutter Magic system, the plot hooks and the new organizations are among the first things which drew me to Hunter- and actually, the CofD in general. And of course, you can't forget about Dark Eras- which is just amazing on so many levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T17:44:12-07:00","id":1104552,"title":"","content":"For my group (we mainly play Changeling), we get a lot of mileage out of Relics, Second Sight, and Asylum, although there has been more call for Inferno of late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T17:59:21-07:00","id":1104558,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of Blue Books. Slasher, Inferno and Book of the Dead more than the others, as they are awesomeness and horror distilled in single volumes (I can't help but to regularly get back and read those again from time to time), but others like Reliquary, Asylum and Second Sight are also a favorite. Blue books in general are what gives CoD personality without having to resort to gamelines. They really sell the differences between CoD and WoD.<br /> <br /> I also have favorite books among the gamelines. Predators is where Forsaken really clicked for me, showing me the true horror of the spirit world and the Shartha, one of my greatest CoD loves. Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss is another gem that I must have read dozens of times. Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead is one of the best of the Night Horrors line (and that's saying something) and I won't waste words to explain why Requiem For Rome is great. Saturnine Nights gave us the Zeka. Witch Finders, as LostLight said, is a really solid book, probably the culmination of the &quot;Enemy&quot; Hunter books.<br /> <br /> And then there's Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> EDIT: if we include fiction books to this, the Beast, Promethean and Werewolf anthologies are really good. Though, as I'm writing this, I realize they're about my favorite gamelines and thus I'm quite biased, I do really think they're the best ones so far. Can't wait for the Changeling one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-24-2017, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T18:02:56-07:00","id":1104559,"title":"","content":"Favorite core book? Mage 2E. The Free Council is my favorite organization in the WoD, I like the themes of mystery and obsession in Mage, and I just like being able to play a modern wizard.<br /> <br /> Favorite Blue Book? Changing Breeds, just for the idea of off-brand were-beings, even if some of the execution and thematics might have been off. I think they may have actually gone too far in the direction of codified splat-building rules, when I think a few template splats for players and STs to modify might have worked better, but I still thought it was a neat book, and I'd love to see it and Skin-Changers make it into 2E. Plus, in my Werewolf games, non-Uratha children of Father Wolf exist, and they'renot terribly big fans of the Forsaken or the Pure, despite sometimes being part of their Packs.<br /> <br /> Favorite Non-Blue Supplement? That's a toughie, but I'd have to say Heirs to Hell. It's interesting that the splat that is most likely to discard personal connections is the one that got the most exploration of their children in a book, and just mechanically the Offspring are neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:29:26-07:00","id":1107473,"title":"","content":"Because I'm an idiot, I forgot about a thing: <b>Innocents</b>.<br /> <br /> Really, it did not cross my mind because it's basically another core, but that book is a masterpiece. I'm partial because kids in horror are a thing that taps into my childhood memories and a subgenre I'll love forever, but Innocents is wonderfully written, inspiring, enlightening and can frankly be used to run CoD without anything else. I have used it to run some short campaigns that, even with all my years as Storyteller, are among the most memorable and loved ones<br /> <br /> I remember getting emotional at some points while reading it. God, what was I thinking when I did not mention it? If I could facepalm myself as hard as I'd want to right now, I'd erase my face","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:48:02-07:00","id":1108172,"title":"","content":"Armory, Asylum, Innocents, almost all of Hunter, and the Changeling core book, for overall usefulness, fun ideas and interesting concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T22:38:32-07:00","id":1108282,"title":"","content":"Not sure if any of these three stand out above each other but Imperial Mysteries for being one of the books that got me back into Mage while being the to date best book I ever read on high level play. Left Handed Path for again bringing me back to Mage and it's been a while since I read it but I remember finding the prose in it a massive and enjoyable departure from the core's dry text. Finally Hunter the Vigil for being one of the surprises of the, then, NWoD early days. That book made me want to immediately play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T05:06:02-07:00","id":1108355,"title":"","content":"Hunter is my personal favorite splatbook. I am also a big fan of Skinchangers, Second Sight, and Inferno for talking about some familiar weirdness that can exsist independant of the playable monsters. Reliquary is great and I really like the ideas behind Mummy as intimidating as it is for me to consider running or even playing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13584-horace-tabor","name":"Horace Tabor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13584_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}